.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-SLOT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-slot
.Nd update the root filesystem that is not running
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | sync | update | switch | rollback | confirm
.Nm
.Cm install Ar package No ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
On a machine installed with
.Nm novi-install Fl -ab
there are two root slots and a shared state partition.
.Nm
applies a change to the slot that is
.Em not
running and points the bootloader at it, so nothing is ever modified
underneath a running system and undoing a change costs one reboot
rather than a restore.
.Bl -tag -width "install pkg ..."
.It Cm status
Which slot is running, which boots next, whether the inactive slot is
populated, and whether a trial boot is in flight.
.It Cm sync
Make the inactive slot a copy of the running one.
The slot is emptied first: a slot is a copy, not the union of every
sync ever made into it.
.It Cm install Ar package No ...
Install packages into the inactive slot, seeding it first if it is
empty.
.It Cm update
Update the inactive slot's packages.
.It Cm switch
Boot the inactive slot next time, as a
.Sy trial :
if that boot does not reach a userland, the boot after it returns here
on its own.
.It Cm rollback
The same operation, named for the direction somebody is going when
they need it.
It does
.Em not
arm a trial, because a rollback is a decision rather than an
experiment, and it clears one that is already armed.
.It Cm confirm
Clear a trial in flight.
.Pa rc.init
does this on every boot; it is not normally run by hand.
.El
.Ss What a confirmed trial claims
That the slot reached a userland which got as far as boot convergence,
and no more.
Whether the update was any
.Em good
is a judgement nothing here makes.
If you boot it and do not like it, roll back.
.Ss What is shared and what is not
.Pa /home ,
.Pa /var/log ,
.Pa /var/lib/novi-state ,
.Pa /var/lib/alsa
and
.Pa /var/cache/pkg
are on the shared state partition and survive a switch.
.Pa /var/lib/pkg
is the slot's own package database and deliberately is not shared.
.Pp
.Pa /etc
is the slot's own.
It holds the boot script and the generated service database, so it
cannot be shared; the cost is that a change made here since the last
.Cm sync
is not in the other slot, and
.Cm switch
and
.Cm rollback
name the files that differ before you reboot.
Accounts are part of that: a user created on one slot has a home
directory on the shared partition that the other slot can see and has
no name for.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/novi/slot-synced" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/slot-synced
Written last by
.Cm sync ,
removed first.
Its presence is what makes a slot bootable rather than half-copied.
.It Pa /boot/grub/grubenv
Holds
.Va novi_slot
and
.Va novi_try .
See
.Xr novi-grubenv 8 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Put two packages on the other slot and boot it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-slot install sqlite man
# novi-slot switch
# reboot
.Ed
.Pp
Go back:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-slot rollback
# reboot
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-install 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr novi-grubenv 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0041,
.Pa /usr/share/doc/novi/rfcs/0041-atomic-updates-and-rollback.md .
.Sh CAVEATS
Encrypted installs cannot use A/B yet:
.Nm novi-install
refuses
.Fl -ab
together with
.Fl -encrypt .
